{
  "rationale": "Evidence: the iteration-0 design went off track in all 60 development trials (finish rate 0). Progress was only 0.04 to 0.12, so the robot left the line within about 0.5 m. RMS error (0.03 m) was small and steering oscillation was low (0.06 to 0.07), so the robot was not jittering. The failure is a lost-line problem. The sensors span only x = ±0.04 m, and the tape edge leaves that span at roughly 0.05 m off-centre, where the sum of readings drops below 0.05 and line loss begins. Max error reached 0.061, right at the off-track limit of 0.06 m, so the robot drifted out during line loss or a tight bend. Steering gain (kp=2) was also too weak to pull back from a large error quickly.\n\nChanges: (1) Widen the sensor span to x = -0.08 to +0.08 m (five sensors at -0.08, -0.04, 0, 0.04, 0.08, y = 0.05), so the tape stays visible at larger lateral errors and line loss happens later. (2) Use sensor_size 0.016 m, a larger footprint that keeps the reading sum above the 0.05 threshold at greater offsets. (3) Scale weights to match the spacing, [-2, -1, 0, 1, 2], so signal ≈ lateral error / 0.04 m and the steering scale is unchanged for near-centre tracking. (4) Raise kp from 2.0 to 3.0 for stronger correction, and raise kd from 0.05 to 0.15 to damp the faster response. Keep ki = 0 to avoid windup on bends. (5) Lower base_speed from 1.4 to 1.2 so the robot has more time to correct on the bends. Finishing is worth far more than speed (500 for completion versus at most 60 for time), so I accept a slower run. (6) Keep line_loss = last_direction, which suits the curves. Body and wheel geometry stay as before, since body width cannot widen the off-track limit beyond 0.06 m.\n\nExpected result: the robot should hold the line through the oval and s-bend and make much further progress, with some chance of completion. Line-loss events should fall to 0 or near 0. I expect RMS error to stay near 0.02 to 0.03 m. If the new gains cause oscillation, the revision should lower kp or raise kd.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.08, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": -0.04, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.04, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.08, "y": 0.05}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.016,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.16,
    "mass": 0.8
  },
  "controller": {
    "base_speed": 1.2,
    "kp": 3.0,
    "ki": 0.0,
    "kd": 0.15,
    "sensor_weights": [-2.0, -1.0, 0.0, 1.0, 2.0],
    "line_loss": "last_direction"
  },
  "observation_request": {
    "measurements": ["completion", "progress", "completion_time", "rms_error", "max_error", "line_loss_events", "steering_oscillation", "control_effort"]
  },
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Wider sensors, higher kp",
      "notes": "Widens the sensor span to ±0.08 m with 16 mm footprints and raises kp to 3.0 with kd 0.15, because the iteration-0 robot lost the line at about 0.05 m off-centre and left the track on every trial. Speed is lowered to 1.2 to give correction time."
    }
  }
}
